    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following the spec, with the helper split into small functions (`_check_item`, `_subtotal`, `_check_coupon_usable`, `_discount`, `_shipping`) so each stays low in cyclomatic complexity and the CRAP score stays under 10. `CouponError` and the signature are unchanged. I wrote 38 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering the rules: item validation, the 100.00 free-shipping boundary, shipping computed after the discount, percent and fixed coupons with their bounds, expiry on the last day, used codes, the minimum subtotal, rounding half-up, and the empty order. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (38 passed). I did not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates, since those tools weren't part of the allowed commands. Two choices the spec left open: I reject `bool` quantities as non-integers, and I check coupon validity (including `kind`) before validating the coupon's `value`.",
